  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">SET ANSI Command &#160;(FoxPro)</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__FoxProOnly" inline="false"/><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Determines how strings of different lengths are compared in SQL commands. This is the FoxPro version of the <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_ANSI">SET ANSI</link> command.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">SET ANSI ON | OFF | &amp;&lt;cMacro&gt;</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ON | OFF<tab />ON pads the shorter string with blanks before the comparison. OFF compares the strings up to the length of the shorter string. The value may also be a macro (&amp;) that evaluates to ON or OFF.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Remarks</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">In the FoxPro dialect the command changes the SQL specific setting Set.SqlAnsi. The runtime does not use this setting at this moment. The generic <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_ANSI">SET ANSI</link> command in the other dialects changes the setting Set.Ansi, which controls the use of the ANSI or OEM character set.</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibVFP" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_ANSI">SET ANSI</link>, <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SET_EXACT">SET EXACT</link></para>
  </body>
